An optimal and elegant solution in JavaScript for **Maximum Binary String After Change**.

### Method Explanation

The problem allows two operations:
1. `"00" -> "10"`: Combines two zeros into a `'1'` and a `'0'`. This reduces the total count of zeros by 1.
2. `"10" -> "01"`: Moves a zero to the left past a `'1'`.

To maximize the binary string:
1. We want as many `'1'`s as possible, and we want any `'0'`s to be as far to the right as possible.
2. Since `"10" -> "01"` moves zeros to the left, all zeros that appear after the first `'0'` can be moved leftward until all zeros form one contiguous block right after the leading `'1'`s.
3. If there are $k$ zeros in total:
   - If $k \le 1$, no `"00" -> "10"` operation can be performed, so the string cannot be improved (return `binary` as is).
   - If $k \ge 2$, the block of $k$ zeros (`"00...0"`) can be transformed using `"00" -> "10"` repeated $k - 1$ times into $k - 1$ ones followed by a single zero (`"11...10"`).
4. As a result, the final string will have only a single `'0'`, located at index:
   $$\text{first\_zero\_index} + k - 1$$
   Every other position in the string will be `'1'`.

